## Structural Map

Key files Claude reads first:
- `handlers/[main].go` — HTTP entry point, request parsing, auth, routing
- `services/[main].go` — Business logic and orchestration (no DB calls here)
- `repository/[main].go` — All database access via GORM
- `models/[main].go` — Struct definitions, no logic

Layers and their purpose:
- `handlers/` → Parse request, validate, route to service (≤50 lines each)
- `services/` → Business logic, orchestration across repos (no direct DB queries)
- `repository/` → All database access via GORM; single DB concern per file
- `models/` → Struct definitions only; no logic, no DB calls
- `middleware/` → Cross-cutting concerns: auth, logging, rate limiting
- `tests/` → Unit tests alongside source (`*_test.go`)
- `cmd/` → Main entry point and wiring

